fixup! Bug 2065519 - Use shared attribute based loader in calendar read dialog. r=#thunderbird-front-end-reviewers

Failure causes:
Job 601478065 exposes a patch-caused disconnect error. The read dialog now clears its data when removed. That cleanup calls setDescription("") after the embedded browser's contentDocument becomes null. The old optional chain guards only the browser, so accessing body throws. The supplied assessment classifies the other 100 jobs as unrelated; no unknown classifications remain.

Changes:
Changed two files: 58 added lines and one removed line. calendar-dialog-description-row.mjs now guards contentDocument in the empty-description branch. A short comment explains the disconnect condition. Normal rendering and the dialog's source cleanup remain intact. browser_calendarDialogDescriptionRow.js adds use strict and test_clearDisconnectedDescription. The test checks connected clearing, repopulates the description, removes the row, checks that the browser document is null, and clears the disconnected row. The actual diff matches both recorded evidence decisions, with no departures. The sourceUpdates revision contains the same affected code, and priorFixup is null. The related Calendar Save-test repair addresses different defects; none of its changes or completed checks were reused.

Validation:
Passed node --check for both changed files, git diff --check, ESLint 9.39.1, and Prettier 3.8.5 --check. Direct ESLint used the current configuration and in-tree Mozilla and SDL plugins with isolated dependencies. Resolved configuration confirms both files are included and the test receives browser-test globals. A syntax-tree audit checked all 20 assertions, including five new assertions; every message is non-empty and contains should. A controlled experiment executing the actual module reproduced the original TypeError before the guard and passed afterward. It also checked cached text and HTML rendering, connected clearing, and repeated clearing without a document. All build and test attempts used AUTOCLOBBER=1. Final Git status contains only the two intended source changes; HEAD is unchanged.

Validation limits:
No native browser test passed. The normal mach test command reported UNKNOWN TEST because the isolated output directory lacks test metadata. The installed headless Mochitest harness then stopped before tests during process enumeration: PermissionError: [Errno 1] Operation not permitted (originated from sysctl() malloc 1/3). Native regression failure-before/pass-after, read-dialog, routing, and accessibility validation remain incomplete. The module experiment uses browser and document stand-ins and does not establish native browser behavior. The available build is marked incomplete and reports SourceStamp=unknown. mach commlint failed dependency installation with EPERM for gecko/node_modules and also reported ambiguous object directories; direct lint success does not establish every wrapper check. The independent evidence assessment remains incomplete. The other 100 job classifications retain their supplied evidence. No files were staged or committed, and no Git refs or shared rules changed. Ignored validation files are excluded.

